Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.86,0:00:04.69,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Sup, nerds! Gobo here!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.69,0:00:07.34,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Here's a recap of \Neverything that's happened so far!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.34,0:00:09.24,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Who are you even talking to?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.70,0:00:18.41,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.41,0:00:21.08,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.08,0:00:25.75,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.30,0:01:43.42,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,It all began on June 5,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.86,0:01:48.62,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,with a mysterious message that appeared \Nbefore Saneatsu Narita as he was in class...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.09,0:01:50.09,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(525,85)\fs17}Two left
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.09,0:01:50.09,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,45)}You are currently looking\Nat this screen
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.84,0:01:55.97,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,What ensued the next day was a series \Nof sudden massive fatalities all over the globe.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.97,0:01:57.69,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Social infrastructure came to a halt.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.56,0:02:03.20,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,After receiving a call from his friend, \NKazuhiko, Saneatsu made his way to school.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.46,0:02:05.86,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,The following day,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.86,0:02:10.90,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,a mysterious figure calling themselves\N the Emperor appeared,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.11,0:02:14.36,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an4\fad(1000,1)}Tasuketsu
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.46,0:02:14.36,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,announcing a cruel death game \Nof majorities called "Tasuketsu".
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.90,0:02:16.80,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,The whole world was forced to participate.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.80,0:02:19.59,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Participants couldn't choose their responses.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.99,0:02:21.00,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(369,20)}Absent
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.59,0:02:25.72,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Their only option was to submit \Nquestions within daily Designated Areas.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.72,0:02:28.75,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,The Emperor would select among \Nthe submissions and conduct a tally.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.75,0:02:30.75,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,89)}Suginami Ward
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.16,0:02:34.88,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Man, all of it was so unfair, \NI felt so helpless and hid myself away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.60,0:02:37.89,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Until I met Ippy-hiko and the guys, that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.89,0:02:39.39,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}June 5
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.39,0:02:41.39,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(568,57)}Two left
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.39,0:02:41.39,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,You are currently looking\N at this screen
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.39,0:02:42.89,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}June 6
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.89,0:02:44.89,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs18\pos(502,93)}One left
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.89,0:02:44.89,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,Japanese citizens living\Nin Tokyo Prefecture
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.89,0:02:46.40,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}June 7
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.40,0:02:48.40,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs17\pos(503,89)}Zero left
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.40,0:02:48.40,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,16)}Test run complete\N Rules will be announced\Ntonight at 23:40
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.40,0:02:49.94,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}June 8
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.94,0:02:51.40,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}Tasuketsu
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.40,0:02:53.40,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}Official Start
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.40,0:02:55.40,Black-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs50\pos(320,31)}The Rights
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.78,0:03:01.33,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1000,1)\pos(483,23)}Prime Right                                    Right
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.11,0:03:02.77,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,The Emperor blabbed on about "making \Ngood use" of Rights and Prime Rights
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.77,0:03:06.77,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,and scattered 65 envelopes\N containing either of the two.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.62,0:03:09.04,Comp small -an9,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,1)\pos(440,48)}Prime Right                     Right
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.77,0:03:09.04,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,As for what was inside...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.47,0:03:11.28,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Nishime, take it away!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.28,0:03:12.45,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You're making {\i1}me{\i0} explain?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.45,0:03:15.61,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I mean, you're an adult! 21 years old, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.61,0:03:16.90,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I'm still in 8th grade, ya know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.90,0:03:19.10,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Make it easy and concise, will ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.10,0:03:21.74,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,I'm not sure age is the issue here...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.74,0:03:24.10,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Fine, if I have to...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.67,0:03:30.02,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Prime Rights are extremely \Npowerful magical powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.30,0:03:34.62,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,But obtaining one requires \Nthe sacrifice a human body part.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.68,0:03:37.64,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,For example, Omi lost \Nhearing in his right ear,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.98,0:03:39.91,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Shinozaki lost his right eyesight,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.91,0:03:42.53,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,and Rika Suzuki lost her right leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.79,0:03:44.54,Board,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs19\fad(380,1)\pos(200,104)\frz335}Right
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.38,0:03:46.71,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Rights, on the other hand, \Ndon't require any sacrifices.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.71,0:03:50.41,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,While less enforceable and powerful than Prime \NRights, they can be effective if used right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.12,0:03:51.04,Board,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fs50\move(316,280,316,45)\c&H54431F&}Die
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.06,0:03:56.72,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,According to a woman named Miwa Isshiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.72,0:04:02.05,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,the Rights fall under three attributes: \NPermission, Transmutation, and Production.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.68,0:04:06.81,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\move(680,65,531,65,25,182)}Permission
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.51,0:04:06.81,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\move(445,65,320,65,25,104)}Transmutation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.05,0:04:06.81,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\move(170,65,110,65,25,65)}Production
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.64,0:04:06.81,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Permission Attribute: Rights that \Nexercise powers relating to approval.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.85,0:04:11.19,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Some examples include the \NRejection Right and Compliance Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.11,0:04:15.63,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,My Presentation Right falls under \Nthe Permission Attribute, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.63,0:04:19.76,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Transmutation Attribute: Rights that \Nbring about certain changes or phenomena.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.11,0:04:20.11,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(531,65)}Permission
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.11,0:04:20.11,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,65)}Transmutation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.11,0:04:20.11,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(110,65)}Production
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.03,0:04:26.41,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Examples include Ryuta's Fusion Right \Nand Shinozaki's Visualization Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.04,0:04:30.54,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(531,65)}Permission
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.04,0:04:30.54,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,65)}Transmutation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.04,0:04:30.54,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(110,65)}Production
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.04,0:04:31.82,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Production Attribute: Prime \NRights that produce phenomena
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.82,0:04:34.78,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,that far surpass those of \Nthe Transmutation Attribute.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.78,0:04:37.80,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,Like Souma's Materialization Right! \NHis powers are crazy!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.33,0:04:41.65,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,However, Rights under the \NProduction Attribute come with risks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.04,0:04:45.09,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,They require the user to announce \Ntheir Prime Right with each use.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.09,0:04:48.03,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,And it drains a huge amount of energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.03,0:04:50.05,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,Souma looks exhausted after every use...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.48,0:04:53.86,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(70,1)\pos(320,50)}Exclusive Prime Right
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.97,0:04:53.86,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,And finally, what's referred to \Nas the "Exclusive Prime Right".
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.98,0:04:53.86,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,1)\pos(325,260)}Parental                                          Authority
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.21,0:04:57.99,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,The Prime Right of Parental Authority\N apparently belonged to Saneatsu, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.62,0:05:00.49,Italics,Nishime,0,0,0,,who knows where he's at right now...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.49,0:05:04.70,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,The strongest Prime Rights are under \Nthe Permission Attribute, ya know!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.70,0:05:08.60,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Omi's quasi-major Prime Right of Rejection \Nand the major Prime Right of Obedience!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.03,0:05:16.11,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,When Tasuketsu killed off all the men, \NOmi used his Rejection Right to survive,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.11,0:05:22.30,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,then submitted a question to revive us \Nso we could make it out alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.41,0:05:26.99,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,At this point, it was midnight on June 10.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.99,0:05:30.66,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,There were 2.21 million survivors in Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.27,0:05:34.23,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,The group then went on to gain \Nnew members and work together
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.55,0:05:38.40,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,to move closer to beating the Emperor \Nand ending Tasuketsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.31,0:05:41.54,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,And finally...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.86,0:05:43.86,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,112)\fs50}June 13
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.86,0:05:45.91,Flashback,Saneatsu,0,0,0,,23:30 PM.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.91,0:05:47.37,Flashback,Nishime/Agatsuma/Hikari,0,0,0,,Feint Operation!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.37,0:05:49.37,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(320,30)}Emperor Assassination Strategy
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.35,0:05:54.25,Flashback,Kazuhiko/Yagihashi/Eren,0,0,0,,Power Station Invasion Operation!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.25,0:05:56.25,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,80)\fs50}Commence
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.25,0:05:59.25,Comp big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,1)\an1\fax-0.4\frz17.75\pos(158,161)}As of this moment,\NTasuketsu has concluded.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.22,0:06:02.26,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,It came with a huge price,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.26,0:06:08.83,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,but we were able to defeat the Emperor, \Nand Tasuketsu came to a close.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.39,0:06:08.14,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(318,160)}As of this moment, Tasuketsu has concluded.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.14,0:06:14.65,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs35\pos(488,118)}Remaining human\Npopulation
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.65,0:06:17.61,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs35\pos(499,135)}1 million people\Nin the greater\NTokyo area
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.61,0:06:21.61,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an4\fs30\pos(14,179)}Rights with unknown          whereabouts
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.61,0:06:24.57,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs35\pos(320,45)}40 Rights
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.57,0:06:27.57,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30\pos(474,135)}Civilization Maintenance\N& Infrastructure
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.57,0:06:31.54,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs35\pos(320,45)}Collapsed
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.15,0:06:39.07,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,There's a lot of blackouts, but \Nwe still have electricity and water.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.07,0:06:42.76,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The phone lines are down... \Nsame with the internet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.16,0:06:47.22,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The only reception we get are \None-way transmissions from the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.22,0:06:50.43,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,But... the radio still works.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.83,0:06:56.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,There was that one weird transmission \Nin code... something about "NS" and "FS".
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.74,0:07:00.07,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So I could use radio waves if I wanted to.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.33,0:07:05.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I think I just got an idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.18,0:07:14.43,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,My Queen, Lady Kisaragi.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.28,0:07:18.76,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,We are nearing distribution time \Nfor the Emperor's message,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.13,0:07:21.50,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,so I turned on the in-house power generators.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.50,0:07:23.96,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,How many times must I tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.34,0:07:30.01,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,The electricity isn't just for distribution \Nof the fake Emperor's messages.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.01,0:07:35.77,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,At the very least, this room where I reign \Nshould be able to use electricity at all hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.77,0:07:37.23,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,As you wish...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.23,0:07:40.24,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Besides, it's too soon \Nfor the title of "Queen."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.24,0:07:43.98,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I cannot become the ruler \Nuntil I lay the Emperor to rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.72,0:08:09.72,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,Hikari coming in with the regular update.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.21,0:08:12.24,Default,Hikari,0,0,0,,Lots of weird stuff but \Nnothing out of the ordinary.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.24,0:08:13.18,Italics,Eren,0,0,0,,Roger that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.06,0:08:17.42,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.42,0:08:19.44,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,What did you want to talk about, Gobo?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.99,0:08:22.69,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I want to leave Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.69,0:08:25.11,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,What?! Is your head screwed on right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.11,0:08:27.15,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,What do you wanna leave Tokyo for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.15,0:08:29.99,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Talking with Nishime got me thinking...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.22,0:08:34.16,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,It's already been a month \Nsince Tasuketsu ended.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.73,0:08:37.66,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,There's no more food left in Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.98,0:08:42.71,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Our only path to survival is to escape Tokyo \Nand make our way around Japan to find food.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.03,0:08:47.69,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,But what will happen \Nif we just up and leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.69,0:08:50.22,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,It'll be the end of Tokyo for real this time!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.22,0:08:51.67,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,You have a point...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.67,0:08:55.71,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Electricity supply is maintained by \NSouma's materialized beasts right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.71,0:08:59.33,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Without Souma, electricity supply in Tokyo \Nwill come to a complete halt.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.33,0:09:03.23,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Meaning it'd be \Na lost civilization, literally.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.23,0:09:07.27,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,But think about it... \NWhere are we headed right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.27,0:09:08.61,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Preserving the peace is great and all,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.61,0:09:10.95,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,but how long are we gonna \Npretend to be the Emperor?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.57,0:09:15.37,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,After looking back on everything, \NI'm not sure what's right anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.04,0:09:17.83,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,"Defeat the Emperor."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.83,0:09:21.67,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I suppose the only thing propelling us \Nforward was that shared mission...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.35,0:09:27.04,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,But without a tangible goal, \Nwe're all left simply exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.84,0:09:30.89,Italics,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Perhaps this is the end of the road...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.38,0:09:36.43,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Hey, Gobo! We've got an \Nincoming signal from tablet D!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.43,0:09:38.97,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,D? It's Ryuta!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.97,0:09:42.89,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,There! That should send the signal to Gobo!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.89,0:09:44.01,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Mm-yup!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.83,0:09:47.23,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Looks like they're working hard every night.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.23,0:09:48.61,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I hope they're holding up okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.92,0:09:51.74,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I can't wait to finally \Ntalk face-to-face again!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.74,0:09:55.78,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Jeez, you two are as carefree as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.78,0:09:57.03,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.03,0:09:58.23,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Mm-ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.09,0:10:04.25,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Well, we've got all this to take home. \NThat should make them happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.25,0:10:07.50,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Let's take flowers to Saneatsu \Nup in the tower, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.97,0:10:10.42,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Yeah, let's do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.29,0:10:14.26,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Umm... Yeah, about that...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.65,0:10:17.26,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Weren't they left up there in the tower?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.26,0:10:20.14,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Are you sure they haven't decomposed by now?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.34,0:10:24.90,Default,Rika,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you forgot...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.28,0:10:28.06,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,W-What's wrong, Gobo?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.06,0:10:30.82,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Don't just sit there in silence, you dummy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.82,0:10:32.99,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Ryuta and the guys are coming back!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.99,0:10:36.60,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Omi and Rika are doing okay too! For real!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.24,0:10:41.39,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Yay! So we get to see them again?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.71,0:10:41.39,Default-Top,Souma,0,0,0,,C'mon! Not in front of—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.67,0:10:45.37,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,And they're bringing food too!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.37,0:10:46.98,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,There aren't many people in the countryside,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.98,0:10:49.56,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,so they haven't touched\N the preserved foods yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.56,0:10:51.67,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,They're bringing fresh vegetables \Nfrom farms, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.67,0:10:55.63,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,T-They're heroes! Thank God!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.63,0:10:56.95,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.95,0:10:59.48,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,They found a clue on what to do next!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.48,0:11:01.77,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,L-Looks like we survived for good reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.77,0:11:03.31,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,So things should look up!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.98,0:11:09.81,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,No way! We only have five minutes until \Ntoday's Emperor announcement, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.81,0:11:13.73,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,This is a tablet for outgoing \Ncommunication. Where's my laptop?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.73,0:11:16.31,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Shoot, I left it charging in the basement!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.31,0:11:19.37,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,This pair just can't get it together.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.58,0:11:23.12,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Can't be helped! We'll use the TV screen!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.12,0:11:25.06,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Nishime, turn on the switch!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.06,0:11:26.04,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Roger that!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.04,0:11:27.72,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Will they make it in time?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.72,0:11:31.46,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Well... worst case scenario, we could \Njust say there's no announcement today.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.46,0:11:34.81,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Come on, guys! Somebody \Ncome up with a message, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.81,0:11:37.43,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I can only come up with \Ninappropriate jokes under pressure!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.43,0:11:39.97,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,That's why I'm saying, why not just skip—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.75,0:11:53.98,Emperor,Raion,0,0,0,,Good evening, this is your Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.73,0:11:57.31,Emperor,Raion,0,0,0,,Time to announce today's results.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.98,0:11:59.98,Show Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(492,245)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.36,0:12:06.18,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,He's back from the dead?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.97,0:12:08.72,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,This can't be real!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.72,0:12:11.78,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,W-What do we do now?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.13,0:12:15.80,Italics,Gobo,0,0,0,,That's impossible... we defeated the Emperor!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.80,0:12:17.07,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Calm down!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.07,0:12:19.26,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,This isn't necessarily the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.26,0:12:20.80,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,And it hasn't come up on our phones!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.80,0:12:21.89,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.42,0:12:24.23,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,It's a TV broadcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.23,0:12:27.18,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,That's it! Display each station's \Nbroadcast screen!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.18,0:12:29.64,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Nishime! Turn on the other TVs!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.63,0:12:32.68,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It's only on TSK Broadcasting?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.09,0:12:34.09,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.89,0:12:39.74,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,What the hell is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.01,0:12:43.66,Default,Eren,0,0,0,,Hey, what about our announcement?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.17,0:12:45.25,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.10,0:12:51.37,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}So no usual Emperor announcement today...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.91,0:12:53.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just as I thought.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.74,0:12:57.13,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The current Emperor saw \Nthe television broadcast tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.55,0:13:00.89,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}And they canceled the usual announcement...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.34,0:13:10.31,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&H291207&\fs18\pos(358,82)}TSK Broadcasting\NOur City of Tokyo
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.66,0:13:05.26,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}This proves that the \Ncurrent Emperor is in Tokyo.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.26,0:13:10.31,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like I thought, this Emperor is different \Nfrom the one that conducted Tasuketsu.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.63,0:13:15.07,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}I only broadcast from here \Nat TSK Broadcasting.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.07,0:13:18.78,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}As long as they notice that, \Nthey'll make a move for sure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.51,0:13:22.54,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Until then, I'll keep this up \Nfor as many days as it takes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.70,0:13:27.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Emperor?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.20,0:13:31.16,georgia,Sign,0,0,0,,{\3c&HFAECD8&}Welcome to TSK Broadcasting!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.92,0:13:35.75,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Just kidding. No way they'd be that quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.48,0:13:39.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I'll be waiting, Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.46,0:13:43.47,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,To hear out your truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.92,0:14:17.00,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.37,0:14:20.42,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I'm sure you guys can guess today's agenda.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.88,0:14:24.38,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,And that's the broadcast \Nfrom last night, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.38,0:14:28.60,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You know, I have a feeling \Nwe screwed something up...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.94,0:14:32.38,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Screwed up? You saying I should \Nhave my laptop on me at all times?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.38,0:14:33.60,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You're worried about that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.88,0:14:36.76,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,First and foremost, let's state the obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.76,0:14:38.31,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,The Emperor is dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.54,0:14:44.53,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,As the ones who fought him, \Nwe're the only ones aware of that fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.18,0:14:48.74,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It's been a month since then, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.87,0:14:53.12,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(321,193)}Good evening, this is your Emperor. \N Today's results are as follows.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.82,0:14:55.14,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,For now, Gobo is disguised as the Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.12,0:14:55.87,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs20\c&HFDEAD0&\1a&H08&}Today's execution has been determined to be Tamataro Yamada \N(age 33), who killed three people in Meguro Ward. Goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.12,0:14:55.87,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs20\pos(368,160)\c&HFDEAD0&\1a&H1A&}Please bear in mind to refrain from evil,\Nand work to live as long as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.14,0:14:57.66,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,to send out scripted distributions \Nto maintain the peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.87,0:14:58.88,Comp big-an8 - closeup blue,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(328,37)\c&HDCDED9&}Please bear in mind to refrain from evil,\Nand work to live as long as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.21,0:15:02.70,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,But after giving it some thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.70,0:15:06.81,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,it's possible that someone \Nhas caught on to our façade.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.96,0:15:12.50,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,As it stands, the current Emperor \Nexecutes criminals on a daily basis.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.02,0:15:17.02,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Most people would assume deceiving \Nthe Emperor would result in their execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.35,0:15:19.35,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Yet they went through with the broadcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.03,0:15:23.65,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You mean they did it because they know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.65,0:15:27.28,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,To top it off, we ended up \Nskipping our announcement.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.74,0:15:29.88,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,We got distracted, and \Nthey probably realized that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.39,0:15:34.59,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,T-That sounds really bad, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.59,0:15:37.90,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,What now? Is it something \Nwe can just ignore?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.90,0:15:41.66,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,S-Sure, why not? If we keep \Nignoring them, I'm sure they'll stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.59,0:15:46.41,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,The only one who'd get assassinated is you, \Nbeing the fake Emperor and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.41,0:15:49.55,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Wait! Ignoring is bad news, for real!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.42,0:15:57.23,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Geez, you're so loud you woke me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.23,0:16:00.36,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Souma! Shouldn't you get some rest?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.36,0:16:02.67,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Hikari is guarding the area...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.67,0:16:05.95,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Eren's always up in arms about \Nsomething, so it can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.95,0:16:08.20,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Why didn't you just wake me up, \NShinozaki-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.68,0:16:11.16,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I'm your best weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.16,0:16:13.17,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,You don't look so well.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.17,0:16:14.87,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Get some more rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.87,0:16:18.31,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,You've been using your Materialization Right \Nto the brink every day...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.31,0:16:20.04,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Don't push yourself too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.04,0:16:22.63,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,We can't afford to lose either you or Gobo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.42,0:16:27.83,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,The Materialization Right is the source \Nof all our necessary materials,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.83,0:16:29.99,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,and your beasts provide essential labor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.99,0:16:32.05,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,Get as much rest as you need.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.71,0:16:35.60,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I'm the only one who can make it happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.60,0:16:37.48,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,There's no way I'd give up that easy—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.48,0:16:39.37,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You've got it all wrong, you macho!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.27,0:16:43.48,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,You gotta rest for all our sake, idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.46,0:16:46.17,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I hear ya...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.72,0:16:49.20,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Hey Shinozaki-san, I got an idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.32,0:16:51.66,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.66,0:16:53.73,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Let's cut to the chase.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.73,0:16:55.47,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,They purposely broadcast to one station
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.47,0:16:58.01,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,so we could narrow down \Ntheir location, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.01,0:17:01.04,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Why not just take the bait and go find them?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.58,0:17:05.74,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,But what if it's a trap?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.74,0:17:07.88,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,We'll cross that bridge when we get to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.39,0:17:13.12,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I can unleash my beast, put \Na materialized transceiver on it,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.12,0:17:16.35,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,and, if there's any danger, we can \Nundo the materialization. How's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.54,0:17:23.76,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Fine. Let's go to the roof.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.76,0:17:26.23,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I'll take a look at the station \Nwith my Visualization Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.23,0:17:27.61,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,Sounds good.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.57,0:17:34.53,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Is Souma okay? Like, for real?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.88,0:17:40.62,Default-Top,Nishime,0,0,0,,{\i1}The key to information control: \NPresentation Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.14,0:17:40.60,Default-Top,,0,0,0,,{\fade(100,0)\bord0\c&HEDF4ED&\pos(320,214)}Borinmaru Gokokuhotenji {3:19}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.01,0:17:43.31,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,{\i1}The key to ground search: \NVisualization Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.75,0:17:47.62,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,{\i1}The key to attack, defense, and \Narsenal: Materialization Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.95,0:17:50.51,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,{\i1}The key to enforcement: Compliance Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.06,0:17:53.41,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,{\i1}This group has all the tools it needs!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.86,0:17:57.26,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,{\i1}My role is to keep things together \Nso it doesn't fall apart...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.15,0:18:02.48,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,I see... they used TV broadcasting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.48,0:18:03.69,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Yes, my lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.47,0:18:07.57,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,What an interesting idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.22,0:18:09.65,Default,Kisaragi,0,0,0,,Very well then...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.12,0:18:25.04,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let's see now... Okay then...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.85,0:18:29.54,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Looks like I better make sure \Nthat this is real.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.54,0:18:31.65,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}How about if I pinch myself?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.42,0:18:34.84,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}What's this? A summoning spell?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.84,0:18:37.93,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}This feels just as surreal as Tasuketsu...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.32,0:18:41.43,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or is this the real Emperor?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.43,0:18:43.52,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shoot, I'm starting to doubt myself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.96,0:18:46.77,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait, something feels off...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.46,0:18:50.76,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it not gonna move?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.76,0:18:53.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Its hair is flowing but... that's it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.74,0:18:56.99,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Um, are you the Emperor's pawn?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.91,0:19:03.88,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Well... if I may, I'd like you to take me—
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.33,0:19:06.04,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}It responded.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.41,0:19:11.17,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I'd like... you to... take me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.63,0:19:13.96,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}So that's what's going on.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.96,0:19:17.00,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's supposed to guide me \Nsomewhere given my request.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.00,0:19:19.85,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or at least that's what \Nit's being commanded to do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.85,0:19:21.60,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs50\pos(70,43)}Take
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.85,0:19:25.59,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}It recognizes that "take" is part of the \Ncommand to "take me to a certain place".{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.60,0:19:28.61,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs50\pos(70,43)}Take me to...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.59,0:19:28.61,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}But technically, the word "take" by itself \Nisn't a complete command.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.99,0:19:32.76,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}It either responds to a strict set of orders \Nor it's unable to make its own decisions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.76,0:19:35.87,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}In other words, a complete pawn. \NBut hang on...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.54,0:19:38.53,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}How can it answer my request \Nto take me somewhere{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.53,0:19:40.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}but have no decision-making abilities?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.14,0:19:42.95,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}That would be an oxymoron.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.95,0:19:45.96,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}What happens if I were someone dangerous?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.32,0:19:49.17,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}If decisions were up to the Emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.92,0:19:54.47,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}they would set a transceiver to \Nmonitor me through visuals or audio.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.47,0:19:57.63,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}So they set this thing up \Njust to drop me off...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.82,0:20:01.14,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll try messing with them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.65,0:20:05.57,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Um... Pardon me! Hello, Mr. Emperor!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.57,0:20:08.26,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Can you hear and see me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.17,0:20:13.42,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Um, as you can see, I'm not armed \Nand I mean no harm!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.95,0:20:17.74,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Sorry if there was no need for me \Nto get fully naked... Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.74,0:20:21.65,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,How did he figure out \Nthere was a transceiver?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.65,0:20:25.08,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Sounds like he assumes we can see him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.08,0:20:26.96,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,So they're unarmed for sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.96,0:20:29.54,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,And butt naked. For real.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.54,0:20:35.51,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Um... I plan to head your way now, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.04,0:20:38.13,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I guess I'll see you soon?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.97,0:20:40.97,Phone,Sign,0,0,0,,If you can see through my lie just now,\Nabandon this beast and send over a second beast.\N\NOnce I confirm you've done this, I'll bring you vital information on the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.95,0:20:47.54,Default,Souma,0,0,0,,I don't sense any danger, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.54,0:20:50.02,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Right. Let's bring him over.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.31,0:20:53.65,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Please take me to where \NMr. Emperor is waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.11,0:20:59.19,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's a good chance \Nthey have no visual on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.57,0:21:03.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}That means I still have \Nplenty of opportunities to lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.40,0:21:10.00,Italics-Top,Raion,0,0,0,,Whoa...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.18,0:21:19.20,Italics-Top,Raion,0,0,0,,This beast has really soft boobs...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.01,0:21:20.01,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,Foreboding
